      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philo%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Along Indian Creek where it meets the Navarro River, Philo hosts KZYX, the valley’s long‑running public radio station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philo%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Philo sits at the heart of Anderson Valley, a celebrated wine region known for its pinot noir and other varietals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philo%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, only two specialty lumber mills in Philo echo the town’s once vigorous timber industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
